-- %% MD | unnamed
# Semi-Structured Data Manipulation
-- %% SQL_RAW | unnamed
mkdir -p /tmp/ducklab
-- %% MD | unnamed
**Semi-structured data** refers to data that does not follow a strict tabular schema or data model. Such data may feature some or all the following properties:
- Composite data structures involving multiple values with a single entry, such as sequences of values and groupings of named values within a single entry
- Flexible schemas, both within composite values and in the shape of data across records
- Nested data, where composite values contain further composite values, enabling the modeling of hierarchical data within individual values
-- %% MD | unnamed
A particularly well-known form of semi-structured data is **JavaScript Object Notation (JSON)**, which you are bound to wrangle at one point or another due to its ubiquity as a data interchange format that's used in all manner of systems, such as web **application programming interfaces (APIs), Internet of Things (IoT)** devices, web browsers, and mobile apps.
-- %% MD | unnamed
DuckDB offers a range of data types, built-in functions, and SQL enhancements for effectively working with semi-structured data.
-- %% MD | unnamed
## Licensing
- The [Query JSON from an API](#query-json-from-an-api) section makes use of the
  [TVmaze API](https://www.tvmaze.com/api) which is licensed by [CC
